  {
    "id": "global/undo-is-one-coalesced-block",
    "buffer": [
      "a1",
      "b2",
      "a3",
      "b4",
      "a5"
    ],
    "cursor": [
      1,
      1
    ],
    "keys": ":g/a/d<CR>uu",
    "groups": [
      ":g/a/d<CR>",
      "u",
      "u"
    ],
    "note": "three discrete groups per harness detail 7 — the :g itself, then TWO separate u presses. Measured against real Vim: a SINGLE u fully restores every deleted line at once (unlike every other multi-step feature here, which mints one undo node per edit), so the second u is a genuine no-op with nothing left below it, not a partial further-undo.\n",
    "encodedKeys": ":g/a/d\ruu",
    "expect": {
      "registers": {
        "1": {
          "type": "V",
          "text": "a5\n"
        },
        "2": {
          "type": "V",
          "text": "a3\n"
        },
        "3": {
          "type": "V",
          "text": "a1\n"
        },
        "\"": {
          "type": "V",
          "text": "a5\n"
        },
        "/": {
          "type": "v",
          "text": "a"
        }
      },
      "buffer": [
        "a1",
        "b2",
        "a3",
        "b4",
        "a5"
      ],
      "cursor": [
        1,
        1
      ],
      "error": "",
      "curswant": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "global/body-move-reorders-scattered-matches",
    "buffer": [
      "x1",
      "keep1",
      "x2",
      "keep2",
      "x3"
    ],
    "cursor": [
      1,
      1
    ],
    "keys": ":g/x/m$<CR>",
    "groups": [
      ":g/x/m$<CR>"
    ],
    "note": "a :m body has a net-ZERO line-count delta (it relocates lines, doesn't add or remove any), which the matched-line tracker's usual K.lineShift path cannot represent at all — found by adversarial review, not by this case alone: an earlier implementation silently mispositioned every match after the first here. Measured against real Vim: each matched line is moved to the end in turn, so the final order of moved lines is their ORIGINAL relative order (x1, x2, x3), not reversed or scrambled.\n",
    "encodedKeys": ":g/x/m$\r",
    "expect": {
      "registers": {
        "/": {
          "type": "v",
          "text": "x"
        }
      },
      "buffer": [
        "keep1",
        "keep2",
        "x1",
        "x2",
        "x3"
      ],
      "cursor": [
        5,
        1
      ],
      "error": "",
      "curswant": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "global/nested-global-with-range-raises-e147",
    "buffer": [
      "x1",
      "y",
      "x2",
      "y",
      "x3",
      "y"
    ],
    "cursor": [
      1,
      1
    ],
    "keys": ":g/x/2,4g/y/d<CR>",
    "groups": [
      ":g/x/2,4g/y/d<CR>"
    ],
    "note": "the INNER :g carries its own explicit range (2,4) — measured against real Vim: this is a genuine catchable error (E147, \"cannot do :global recursive with a range\"), thrown only after the outer loop has already visited every matched line (buffer ends up fully untouched; cursor sits on the LAST matched line, exactly where the outer loop parked it before the final, also-rejected attempt)\n",
    "expectError": true,
    "encodedKeys": ":g/x/2,4g/y/d\r",
    "expect": {
      "registers": {
        "/": {
          "type": "v",
          "text": "x"
        }
      },
      "buffer": [
        "x1",
        "y",
        "x2",
        "y",
        "x3",
        "y"
      ],
      "cursor": [
        5,
        1
      ],
      "error": "Vim(global):E147: Cannot do :global recursive with a range",
      "curswant": 1
    }
  }
]
